  "modified": "2026-11-17T10:39:09Z",
  "details": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * kernel: sctp: stream: fully roll back denied add-stream state (CVE-2026-52929)\n  * kernel: net/mlx5: Fix MCIA register buffer overflow on 32 dword reads (CVE-2026-68293)\n  * kernel: sunrpc: pin svc_xprt across the asynchronous TLS handshake callback (CVE-2026-72222)\n  * kernel: sunrpc: wait for in-flight TLS handshake callback when cancel loses race (CVE-2026-72221)\n  * kernel: smb: client: clear setuid/setgid bit on write with cifsacl/modefromsid/posix extensions (CVE-2026-89638)\n  * kernel: openvswitch: Fix CT limit teardown use-after-free (CVE-2026-89488)\n  * kernel: PCI/sysfs: Add lockdown checks to legacy I/O and memory handlers (CVE-2026-90315)\n\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):  \n\n  * [AlmaLinux10.3z] watchdog: System can panic during reboot when pretimeout is disabled (0) (JIRA:RHEL-255346)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
